"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Ordered\n\n\n\n\n## Review\n\nI originally planned to visit a different cafe, but since all seats were full, I inevitably came to a nearby cafe.  \n\nThere is no dedicated parking lot, so you have to find parking in nearby open spaces on your own.  \nHowever, since it has a cozy rural alley vibe, parking didn't seem too difficult.  \n\nFrom the atmosphere of the cafe, it had a strong impression that the owner had lived in Australia before returning.  \n\nFortunately, there were plenty of seats and it was quiet and peaceful, so I comfortably grabbed a table and placed an order.  \nFor coffee, I ordered an Iced Long Black.  \n\nFor dessert, I wanted to have Tiramisu Cake, but unfortunately it was sold out.  \nInevitably, I ordered the Crème Brûlée Cheesecake recommended by the owner.  \n\nPerhaps because the owner runs the cafe alone, it took quite a while from ordering until the items were served.  \nThis too felt somewhat Australian in a way.  \n\nThe long black that came out after the long wait was delicious as expected.  \nThe shape of the cup was a bit unique, and it felt surprisingly nice in the hand.  \n\nThe Crème Brûlée Cheesecake was also just as delicious as the owner had recommended.  \n\nThe weather was so hot that I couldn't even think of stepping outside.  \nThanks to that, I spent a long, leisurely time sitting in the cafe.  \n\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"